  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If \\(f(x)=5x^2-2x-1,\\) then \\(f(x+h)-f(x)\\) equals:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(5h^2-2h\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(10xh-4x+2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(10xh-2x-2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(h(10x+5h-2)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(3h\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1954-p16.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Expanding and canceling gives \\[ \\begin{gathered} f(x+h)-f(x)\\\\ =5(x+h)^2-2(x+h)-1\\\\ {}-(5x^2-2x-1)\\\\ =10xh+5h^2-2h\\\\ =h(10x+5h-2). \\end{gathered} \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Substitute \\(x+h\\) into the polynomial before subtracting \\(f(x)\\)",
        "After cancellation, factor out \\(h\\)"
      ],
